attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 36, `ygeA` to `fucI`, are carried by 93 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 23% of calls {S1}. The model names 7 to 100% of them, fewest at column 7, `ygdR`, 7% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column follows**, column 37, `fucP`, shell, carried by 85% {S2.c37}. Then columns 38 to 53, `fucA` to `rlmD`, are [[fucose and glucarate catabolism]], carried by 90 to 95% {S3, Q}. Through columns 60 to 62 a branch of 3 shell families runs in 11 to 15%, a parallel path some chromosomes carry instead {S4.b60}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.19 against 0.45 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 60, `ygcG`, a fork column, 1.29 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `cys` and `cas` genes**, columns 74 to 79, [[assimilatory sulfite reductase]] {S4.c64-76, Q}. The last column is `casB`, in 20% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.28 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.83 against 0.14 bits, and names fewer genes, 85% against 95% {C}.

